WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.980
Let me ask you this, then.

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.730
...According to your statement...

00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:09.140
When Inspector Oda fired
at the group of serial killers,

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.860
a bullet accidentally hit Ms. Cecil,
who was being held hostage.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:16.620
You tried to get Ms. Cecil to the hospital,

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.620
but Inspector Oda
wouldn't let you leave.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.500
Yes.

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:23.500
Since he didn't want to lose
his job as an officer of the law,

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.960
he tried to kill you and Ms. Cecil.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:27.900
Is that correct?

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.960
Mr. Oda tried to kill us with an
...explosive that one of the suspects had—

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:32.880
However,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.510
you're the only one who claims he
planned to kill you with those explosives.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:41.640
Ms. Cecil, who'd been shot,
can't recall the incident, correct?

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.200
Due to a lack of evidence, this should
be considered excessive self-defense.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:47.480
Rather,

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.300
you killed the inspector
...with clear homicidal purpose—

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.320
That isn't true!

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.130
...Mom...

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.130
...Cecil...

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:55.240
Mom wouldn't do that!

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.240
Order!

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:00.940
Now, for closing arguments
and sentencing recommendations.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:09.400
In this trial, the deciding factor is
whether the defendant, Sudou Megumi,

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.210
<i>did indeed kill the victim,
Inspector Oda Kyousuke, in self-defense.</i>

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:16.750
At 2:20 PM, on said day,

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:23.110
the defendant and her daughter, Cecil,
visited the home of Cecil's friend, Oda Akua.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:26.860
Oda Akua is Inspector Oda's son.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.000
At 3:02 PM,

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.340
the group of serial killers responsible
for the murder of judges within the city

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.610
had barricaded themselves
inside Oda's apartment.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.410
Inspector Oda pursued the suspects.

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:44.370
One of the shots Inspector Oda
had fired hit Sudou Cecil.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.650
In retaliation, Sudou Megumi
used fire magic, killing Inspector Oda.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:55.880
It is believed that Inspector Oda had no
murderous intent toward the Sudou family.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.380
This incident concerns a cruel homicide.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:01.890
Therefore, I am requesting
the death penalty.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:07.040
Defense, do you have
any closing arguments?

00:02:12.370 --> 00:02:13.650
I do not.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:17.070
...This isn't what happened...

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:20.460
I will now read the verdict.

00:02:21.180 --> 00:02:25.700
The defendant, Sudou Megumi,
is sentenced to death.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.130
...No...

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:35.510
Mom!

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.420
Why?!

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.850
I will carry my indomitable hope into the dark night

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:44.850
yami no naka no shinjitsu ga hikari kagayaku you ni

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:51.150
so that it may light a shining fire of truth there

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:51.150
kagi no nai kibou wo tokihanatou

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:07.000
I was born bleeding from my hands,

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:07.000
naze te no hira no kizu wo daite umareochita imi

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.620
and why was I born not a thousand years in the past or the future,

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.620
sennen kako demo mirai demo naku

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.080
but in the present?

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.080
erabareta ima

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.130
The scales of justice are fragile

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.130
zen'aku hakaru tenbin wa zeijaku

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:21.510
The waning, waxing moon calls to a flower on the earth

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:21.510
michikakeru tsuki ga izanau gisei no chi ni saita

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.260
the color of blood

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.260
chi no iro no hana

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.740
I will give all I have

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:25.740
tatta hitotsu kanau nara

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.440
if it means one of my wishes will come true

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:28.440
subete wo sasageyou

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.600
I have a "post nubila phoebus" kind of personality

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.600
post nubila phoebus kokoro

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.570
which I will show the world

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.570
kaze ni hanate

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.570
I want to slash apart the curtain of raven black,

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:36.570
shikkoku no curtain hikichigiri

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.260
and look at a new world

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.260
chigau sora wo mitemitai

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.930
I put my love into the cracks

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.930
sabita unmei no hibiware

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.400
of a stagnant fate

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:44.400
omoi wo nejikonde

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.260
No matter how long the storm lasts,

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.260
donnani arasoi tsuzuketemo

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.870
time itself will not stop breathing

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.870
toki wa kokyuu wo yamenai

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.630
What remains after destruction, rebirth,

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.630
kowashite tsunde kowashite

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.100
and further destruction?

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.100
nani ga nokoru darou

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.830
I'm sure the starlit sky can put an end

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.830
sou nanajuuoku mo no mayoi hoshi

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:00.970
to the system of the world

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:00.970
sono haichizu wa kakikaerareru

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.590
I'm sure that one day I will find a place where I can shine

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:03.590
moetsukitemo kagayakeru basho he

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:07.910
even if only ashes will remain

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:07.910
itsuka tadoritsukeru

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:18.520
He said if I could draw out your dormant magic,
then my father's sentence would be reduced.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.190
Draw out my magic?

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.780
But why?

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.660
I don't know the details.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:29.780
But apparently, it has to do
with the incident six years ago.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.960
<i>What was she talking about?</i>

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:36.670
Case 9

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:36.670
Secret Puzzle

00:04:32.510 --> 00:04:35.960
<i>What does my magic
have to do with that case?</i>

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:43.540
Was there anything questionable about
the people involved in your case six years ago?

00:04:43.540 --> 00:04:44.420
Huh?

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:48.060
The wizard barrister or the
prosecutor... or even the judge.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.120
Was there anything off about them?

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:57.100
Well, they <i>did refuse to
listen to my statement.</i>

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:01.560
But that was because my wizard
barrister was incredibly unreliable.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:03.110
Just give me something!
Anything will do!

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.530
Try to remember!

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.520
...Please...

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:10.160
Cecil, what's wrong?

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.810
...Oh, well...

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:15.870
Metropolitan Police Department

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:34.560
Butterfly Law Offices

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:38.940
I've gathered you all here to
discuss what happened in Boston.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:43.190
Since then, I've had Kynt
look into Diana's background.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:47.570
She stole the history and identity of
someone who was already deceased.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:51.540
So the identity of
...whoever was behind this...

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:53.800
We still don't know.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.580
It'll probably be faster to
research the meaning of "Macal",

00:05:57.350 --> 00:06:00.120
since Diana mentioned it.

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:03.090
...Grimoire 365...

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:06.980
That's a book with information
about wizards, right?

00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:09.020
It's just a rumor, though.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:11.510
We should at least
look for it and find out.

00:06:11.510 --> 00:06:14.170
Maybe we'll be able to
discern their motives.

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:15.280
No!

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:20.980
It's too dangerous to make any moves
without knowing their identity.

00:06:21.430 --> 00:06:23.890
Why don't we request
police protection?

00:06:23.890 --> 00:06:27.490
Unless we have something more solid
on this incident, they won't do anything.

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.020
We're wizards.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:33.430
If it ever comes down to it,
we can protect ourselves.

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:35.870
Even if it ends violating
the magic-prohibition law?

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:36.680
Hey.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:39.160
What do you think, Hotaru?

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:40.020
Huh?

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:43.730
...I...

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:48.340
At any rate, for the time being,
don't act on your own.

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:51.130
...Stay on your toes...

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:52.200
Sorry I'm late!

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:54.680
Cecil!

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.060
I told you we had an
important meeting today.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:00.110
I'm sorry... My plans ran
...a bit longer than scheduled...

00:07:00.110 --> 00:07:02.460
Why didn't you contact us, then?

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.530
You're not a student anymore!

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:06.810
If you can't even manage this,
what will you do?

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:11.040
Take more responsibility
for your actions.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:13.550
You're already enough
of a troublemaker.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.080
...I'm sorry...

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.580
Isn't that going a bit far?

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:18.830
Huh?

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:22.080
While Cecil <i>is at fault for being late,</i>

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:25.840
I think you're being a
bit too dramatic, Seseri.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:26.780
Huh?

00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:30.130
Oh, I'm sorry for being impertinent.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.630
...Hotarin just...

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:34.980
...defended Cecilcchi....

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:36.970
I wasn't really defending her!

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:40.280
I just think that all this should be
dealt with a little more rationally.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:43.270
Thank you for defending me.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:46.520
I already said I didn't do it for you.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:48.520
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:49.980
...Okay...

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:50.990
Hey, everyone, check this out!

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:55.820
Supreme Court Chief Justice Makusu
is holding a press conference.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.440
It's about the case from the other day.

00:07:58.440 --> 00:07:59.780
The other day?

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:03.350
You know, the one where a
wizard lied about being human,

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:06.010
who worked as a Ministry
of Foreign Affairs secretary,

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.610
and was sued.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:08.450
...Oh...

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:12.760
<i>So the secretary wasn't held accountable,</i>

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.600
<i>and the judgment found
in favor of the wizards.</i>

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.530
<i>But why was that?</i>

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:22.510
<i>His magic awakened ten years
...after becoming a secretary...</i>

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:25.600
And he continued to fulfill his duties.

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:32.610
I don't believe in using the magic-prohibition
law's article 6 in such an inflexible way.

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:38.440
So you're saying that wizards should be
allowed to hold government positions?

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.810
Do you think article 6
should be amended?

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.620
...I wouldn't go that far, but...

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:47.400
Wizards are full-fledged citizens.

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:52.440
They've always been persecuted
on countless occasions.

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:55.380
Just because they're wizards,
they've faced discrimination.

00:08:55.910 --> 00:08:59.360
And I believe that sealing away their magic,
their very symbol of existence,

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:01.390
would be rather hard on them.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:05.020
As a human, I feel for them.

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:11.770
There is popular belief that the magic-prohibition
law's article 6 is fairly discriminatory.

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:17.030
From here on, I believe humans and
...Wuds must learn to work together...

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:21.060
<i>Even within legal circles.</i>

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:23.450
A Wud as a government official?

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.190
You've gotta be kidding me.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:28.330
I'm throwing in my badge if that happens.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:32.240
It's best that you not
look down on Wuds too much.

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.060
Huh?

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:37.840
Oh, just that... I think you're much
scarier than Wuds, Inspector Quinn.

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.970
What the hell are you saying?

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:45.140
...Huh? Cecilun...

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.270
You're not supposed to
act on your own, remember?

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:49.700
...U-Um, um...

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.150
That isn't what it looks like.

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:53.690
I'm working!

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:57.190
Oh, okay. Well, have fun.

00:09:57.190 --> 00:09:59.700
...S-See you later...

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:03.950
You shouldn't lie.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.080
You should at least tell Moyo the truth.

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:10.830
It was scary how she
saw right through me.

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:13.540
Moyo likes you a lot.

00:10:14.230 --> 00:10:17.050
I'm sorry I lied to you, Moyoyon.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.770
...About when you were in Canada...

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:23.820
Did Cecil tell you anything?

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:24.550
Huh?

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:26.750
...So you heard...

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:28.830
about her mother.

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:33.090
But I have no intention of pitying her.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:35.820
Work is work.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:36.770
...But...

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:41.870
I had no idea how heavy
Cecil's burden was.

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:46.080
If there's anything I can do,

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:47.580
I'd like to help her.

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:53.670
Okay.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:57.310
The chief is out on an important matter.

00:10:57.310 --> 00:10:58.050
Huh?

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:03.020
I'm terribly sorry. Could you
return another time, perhaps?

00:11:03.020 --> 00:11:05.850
What? But I had an appointment.

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:07.190
Please leave.

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:10.970
Fine.

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:20.410
No luck with the wizard
barrister or the prosecutor.

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:22.310
That only leaves the judge.

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:27.710
No one's gonna want to discuss
a six year old case.

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:31.030
But I have to get some kind of evidence.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.340
Building 1 ・  Building 2

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.890
I heard a female wizard
barrister was here for me,

00:11:34.890 --> 00:11:37.340
...so I came down to see...

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.930
But I never expected you to be so young.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:41.470
Well?

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:45.650
What was it you wanted, Tentou Moyo?

00:11:46.530 --> 00:11:49.420
I'm sorry. That isn't my name.

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:50.230
Huh?

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:52.200
My name's Sudou Cecil.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:56.740
I figured that, if I gave you my
real name, you wouldn't talk to me.

00:11:57.410 --> 00:11:58.940
...Sudou...

00:12:01.370 --> 00:12:03.030
...From six years ago...

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:05.450
Let me get straight to the point.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:09.610
Was there not something improper

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:11.510
...about my mother...
Sudou Megumi's trial?

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:13.880
What are you talking about?

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:16.820
I know this is a bit rude,

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:19.770
...but... I just...

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.890
I want you to tell me the truth.

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:24.030
...That trial—

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:25.140
This is rude!

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:28.270
What evidence do you have to
support a claim of impropriety?

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:33.930
I always produce a verdict that
objectively reflects the presented evidence.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:35.400
The same was true of that trial.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:37.150
...B-But...

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.990
"Innocent until proven guilty."

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:44.650
That wasn't really upheld, was it?

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.790
I always act fairly!

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:49.660
If you plan to question
that judgment any further,

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.470
then I don't hold back
just because you're a child.

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:54.030
I'm not a child!

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.500
I am involved in this case!

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:01.890
Maybe for you, this was simply
...another case, but for my mother and me...

00:13:02.480 --> 00:13:04.140
Our lives are at stake!

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.390
I have nothing to say to you.

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:09.140
Get out!

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:13.920
Well, that judge is right.
We need evidence.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:17.150
This hasn't changed
anything from before.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.760
I know there's some kind
of answer right in front of me,

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.340
but I just can't grab hold of it.

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:25.670
Change up your investigation method.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:28.400
If you keep going at it head-on,

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:31.040
you'll only be rejected over and over.

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.660
...You're right...

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:35.530
...The only person I can rely on now is...

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:38.550
How surprising.

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:41.690
I didn't expect you to contact me.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:44.870
I'm sorry to bother you
...when you're busy, but...

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:46.450
...I didn't have...

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:48.560
anyone else I could turn to.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.060
Well? What do you need?

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:58.150
Want to get one?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.070
Huh?

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:03.860
You really need to
work your legs for this.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:05.070
...Um...

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:08.440
Well, I thought it'd be
easier to talk like this.

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:11.540
We won't have anyone
interrupting us, either.

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:16.400
I see.

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:20.110
So you're reinvestigating
the case on your mom.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:22.730
Around the precinct,
...it was a pretty famous case...

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:25.510
Given that the victim was a cop.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:31.950
Shizumu... As a police officer,
what do you think of that judgment?

00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:35.450
You like to cut straight
to the point, huh?

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:37.870
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:43.210
As a fellow police officer,
I couldn't stand what happened back then.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:47.470
But I think that only those
who were there know the truth.

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.330
...However...

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.960
Sometimes ignorance is bliss.

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:53.960
Huh?

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:57.960
Well, that's just my opinion.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:01.950
If you want to find some clues,
I'll help you out.

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:05.410
I'll check the investigation files.

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:07.220
You will?!

00:15:07.220 --> 00:15:11.860
It must be really important
for you to come to me about it.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:16.180
And you've helped us
...in capturing suspects, so...

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:18.030
Thank you very much!

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:21.360
I didn't know what I was
going to do on my own.

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:22.820
Thank goodness.

00:15:24.560 --> 00:15:25.540
...Say...

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:26.490
Yes?

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:29.570
What made you want
to look over the case?

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:33.160
...Well, in Boston—

00:15:40.590 --> 00:15:42.830
I'm sorry! Are you all right?

00:15:46.550 --> 00:15:48.560
...That was close...

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:49.590
Are you okay?

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:56.930
Y-Y-Y-Y-Y-Yes!

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:08.110
So you were looking into
that incident from six years ago.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:08.610
Huh?

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:13.620
I got a call from Professor Shindaiji,
who was the judge on that case.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:16.620
I hear you even used Moyo's name.

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:21.530
I'm sorry for acting on my own
without letting you know.

00:16:24.220 --> 00:16:29.210
Cecil, what do you think
of everyone at Butterfly?

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.140
...Huh? Well...

00:16:33.640 --> 00:16:36.130
Everyone's very skilled
in their own way,

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:39.510
and they work very hard and effectively.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:41.450
That's not what I'm asking you.

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:45.310
You don't have to hold everything in.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:49.150
Everyone in the office
is your friend, Cecil.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:50.900
Don't forget that.

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:52.810
You... are?

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.740
We're here for you.

00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:59.760
There's so many people
who are worried about you.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:02.070
...Ageha...

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:11.950
<i>Glory to Macal.</i>

00:17:11.950 --> 00:17:13.760
<i>Punish Labone.</i>

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:16.260
<i>Prosperity to Macal.</i>

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:20.770
<i>May the humans suffer
many years of pain.</i>

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:28.780
We'll need a lot more
eyes for the ritual.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:31.980
They are offerings for Lucifer,
who loves the light.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:35.030
You said we would keep
sacrifices to the minimum.

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.540
Of course we will.

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:40.490
Only enough to summon Lucifer.

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:44.790
Have you found a way
to activate the catalyst?

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:46.530
Yes.

00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:49.510
Starting six years ago,

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:53.110
everything has been carefully planned,
all for what will happen in four days.

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:57.150
There have been many
sacrifices because of that.

00:17:57.810 --> 00:18:02.310
Should we let this chance slip,
everything we've worked for will be for nothing.

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.810
Don't forget that.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:05.830
Got it?

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.300
<i>I have no choice.</i>

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:18.900
<i>It's for the future of Macal.</i>

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:21.460
Thank you very much.

00:18:22.070 --> 00:18:22.950
Yes.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.750
I'll head over tomorrow.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:27.130
Thank you for your time.

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:31.830
He said he'll give me
the investigation files!

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:35.150
I never thought he'd act so quickly!

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:42.350
Don't go showing your
pervy body to Shizumu.

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:46.900
Like hell I would, you pervy frog!

00:18:47.710 --> 00:18:50.110
Pain is bliss!

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.710
You sure are in a good mood, Cecilun.

00:18:57.710 --> 00:19:00.220
Eh? Does it show?

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:02.770
Oh, boy. I should calm down.

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:04.530
Do you have a date?

00:19:06.110 --> 00:19:08.920
I can't let that statement go
unheard, but just a warning!

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:08.920
Click on the card after inputting information

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:08.920
Sudo
Cecil

00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:10.540
...Your luck today, Cecilcchi...

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:12.300
...Awful, horrible...

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.300
Your Luck Today:

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.300
Awful

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.300
Horrible

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:15.760
You're going to be kidnapped!

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:17.840
What are you talking about?

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.510
Don't look into my future
without my permission, Sori!

00:19:20.850 --> 00:19:22.820
Besides, I'm going to be kidnapped?

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:26.720
It could mean that someone
will take your heart.

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.280
Wait. Hang on.

00:19:29.280 --> 00:19:34.160
Maybe it was that you'll
end up being touched.

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.660
No one's gonna be touching me!

00:19:41.460 --> 00:19:42.390
Shizumu!

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:45.830
We've been given jurisdiction. Let's go.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:48.500
Go on without me.

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:50.490
I'll meet up with you.

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:51.380
What's wrong?

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:55.550
You're usually the first one
at an investigation meeting.

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:59.890
I'm just going to look
...into the scene a bit more...

00:19:59.890 --> 00:20:01.730
Where do you think you're going?

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:05.090
Tell me!

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:07.930
What are you thinking?!

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.220
None of your business.

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:10.150
Huh?

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:12.150
It's none of your business!

00:20:15.970 --> 00:20:17.190
...Shizumu...

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:19.160
Morino Bowl

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:26.670
Oh! Shizumu!

00:20:31.310 --> 00:20:32.540
Run.

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:37.050
Wai— What's going on?

00:20:37.050 --> 00:20:39.090
I'll tell you later. Just run!

00:20:39.090 --> 00:20:40.140
Why?!

00:20:40.140 --> 00:20:42.100
If he catches you, you're done for!

00:20:42.100 --> 00:20:44.170
I don't understand
...what you're saying...

00:20:49.900 --> 00:20:51.070
Come on!

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:54.550
No! Why do I have to run?!

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:58.210
Shizumu?

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:06.070
Look out!

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:14.210
...<i>Shizumu is...</i>

00:21:14.990 --> 00:21:16.630
<i>a wizard?</i>

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:20.610
Hurry up!

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:34.060
Do you get it now?
Do you see who he is?

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:35.950
...Why did Shizumu...

00:21:36.760 --> 00:21:38.070
Why?

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:39.560
He's after you.

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:42.620
Huh?

00:21:50.390 --> 00:21:52.160
Where should I even begin?

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:57.260
This plan started six years ago.

00:21:58.300 --> 00:21:59.940
Six years ago?!

00:21:59.940 --> 00:22:02.010
Plan? What plan?

00:22:02.620 --> 00:22:06.050
Six years ago, on that day,

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:07.750
you died.

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:10.060
Eh?

00:22:26.210 --> 00:22:33.510
Tears may drench the skies of my heart,

00:22:26.210 --> 00:22:33.510
kokoro no sora ni namida afuretemo

00:22:33.510 --> 00:22:40.880
but I still want to behold the blue outside

00:22:33.510 --> 00:22:40.880
hitomi ni aozora utsushiteitai

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:48.270
I want to have something like the strength of flowers

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:48.270
concrete-iro no machi no katasumi ni

00:22:48.270 --> 00:22:55.690
which bloom in the nooks of the endless concrete of the city

00:22:48.270 --> 00:22:55.690
sotto saku hana no tsuyosa wo manetai

00:22:55.690 --> 00:23:03.230
Starting today, I won't try to wriggle out by saying

00:22:55.690 --> 00:23:03.230
maegami ga jama de mienai nante iiwake

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:07.490
that I saw nothing because my hair was in the way

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:07.490
kyou kara shinai

00:23:07.910 --> 00:23:15.420
Beyond the horizon, my future awaits me,

00:23:07.910 --> 00:23:15.420
chiheisen no mukou ni ashita ga matteru kara

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:20.630
so I will let the sun in my heart

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:20.630
kono mune mou hitotsu no taiyou

00:23:20.630 --> 00:23:22.680
shine out far and wide

00:23:20.630 --> 00:23:22.680
tooku hanatte

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:30.060
I will overtake the earth's rotation on the path I walk,

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:30.060
chikyuu no jiten wo oikosu kurai hitamuki ni arukou

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:38.290
with trusting love inside my heart

00:23:30.060 --> 00:23:38.290
shinjiru omoi dakishimete doko made mo
